hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16815","He said: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Kathir al-Dari narrated to me from Mujahid, he said: An old man who had lived through the pre-Islamic period narrated to us while we were in the campaign of Rhodes, called Ibn Abs, he said: I was driving a cow belonging to a family of ours, he said: And I heard from its belly: O Al Dharih, an eloquent saying, a man shouting: There is no god but Allah. He said: So we came to Mecca and found that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had emerged in Mecca."
